From: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] can: gs_usb: support up to 4 CAN interfaces

The RoboParty USB-to-CANFD adapter exposes four CAN channels. The vendor
4.14 driver caps the number of interfaces per device at two, so the third
and fourth channels are rejected during probe. Raise GS_MAX_INTF to four.

This mirrors the vendor SDK change carried as
roboparty_rdk/build_params/gs_usb.patch (which raises the X5 6.1 driver from
three to four); the X3 4.14 driver starts at two, hence 2 -> 4 here.

Signed-off-by: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c b/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/can/usb/gs_usb.c
@@ -159,9 +159,9 @@
 /* Only launch a max of GS_MAX_RX_URBS usb requests at a time. */
 #define GS_MAX_RX_URBS 30
 /* Maximum number of interfaces the driver supports per device.
- * Current hardware only supports 2 interfaces. The future may vary.
+ * Current hardware only supports 4 interfaces. The future may vary.
  */
-#define GS_MAX_INTF 2
+#define GS_MAX_INTF 4
 
 struct gs_tx_context {
 	struct gs_can *dev;
-- 
2.43.0
